                  <widget class="QLabel" name="lbl_orbit">
                   <property name="text">
                    <string>Orbital elements</string>
                   </property>
                  </widget>
                 </item>
                 <item row="3" column="1" colspan="2">
                  <widget class="QLineEdit" name="lineEdit_orbit">
                   <property name="toolTip">
                    <string>File with the seven orbital elements (P, e, K_A, K_B, gamma, T_peri, omega in rad), one per line, in the work folder. Start values of the orbit mode; the orbit optimisation writes its best elements back to it. Used by the Editor and the orbit fit (Tools) as well.</string>
                   </property>
                  </widget>
                 </item>
                 <item row="4" column="0">
                  <widget class="QLabel" name="lbl_bc">
                   <property name="text">
                    <string>Barycentric correction</string>
                   </property>
                  </widget>
                 </item>
                 <item row="4" column="1">
                  <widget class="QLineEdit" name="lineEdit_bc">
                   <property name="toolTip">
                    <string>File with the barycentric correction BC [km/s] per spectrum (last number of each line, e.g. &lt;prefix&gt;barycorr.txt of Tools -&gt; Barycentric correction); empty: none. Spectra in the observatory frame: the RVs of the orbit are converted to the observatory frame, (1 + v_obs/c) = (1 + v/c) / (1 + BC/c). Barycentrically corrected spectra: the static lines are shifted by BC. Needed for the orbit mode with static lines.</string>
                   </property>
                  </widget>
                 </item>
                 <item row="4" column="2" colspan="2">
                  <widget class="QComboBox" name="comboBox_bcframe">
                   <property name="toolTip">
                    <string>Frame of the spectra: observatory frame (as observed; static lines at rest) or barycentrically corrected (lambda_bary = lambda_obs (1 + BC/c); static lines move by BC).</string>
                   </property>
                   <item>
                    <property name="text">
                     <string>observatory frame</string>
                    </property>
                   </item>
                   <item>
                    <property name="text">
                     <string>barycentric (corrected)</string>
                    </property>
                   </item>
                  </widget>
                 </item>
                 <item row="5" column="0">
                  <widget class="QLabel" name="lbl_tellw">
                   <property name="text">
                    <string>Static line strength</string>
                   </property>
                  </widget>
                 </item>
                 <item row="5" column="1">
                  <widget class="QLineEdit" name="lineEdit_tellw">
                   <property name="toolTip">
                    <string>Start values of the strength of the static lines per spectrum: a file with one value per line, e.g. the airmass (&lt;prefix&gt;airmass.txt of Tools -&gt; Barycentric correction), scaled to a mean of 1. Empty: from edit.dat (Editor) or 1.</string>
                   </property>
                  </widget>
                 </item>
                 <item row="5" column="2" colspan="2">
                  <widget class="QCheckBox" name="checkBox_tellfit">
                   <property name="toolTip">
                    <string>Fit the strength of the static lines per spectrum (telluric lines vary with airmass and water vapour): Solve and the start of an optimisation alternate solving and a least-squares scale per spectrum until the strengths no longer change (at most 10 times); during an optimisation they are kept. Mean 1. Exclude saturated bands (Model tab): their depth does not scale linearly.</string>
                   </property>
                   <property name="text">
                    <string>fit per spectrum</string>
                   </property>
                  </widget>
                 </item>
                 <item row="6" column="0">
                  <widget class="QCheckBox" name="checkBox_tellrange">
                   <property name="toolTip">
                    <string>Solve the static spectrum only in the wavelength ranges of the file (observatory frame), zero elsewhere: fewer unknowns, faster, and no broad structure outside. If the file does not exist, a default with all telluric O2 and H2O systems of the optical (weak ones included) is written to the work folder; edit it, or let "Detect" find the ranges in your data.</string>
                   </property>
                   <property name="text">
                    <string>Static lines only in</string>
                   </property>
                  </widget>
                 </item>
                 <item row="6" column="1">
                  <widget class="QLineEdit" name="lineEdit_tellrange">
                   <property name="toolTip">
                    <string>File of ranges: per line from to [A] (air, observatory frame) and optionally a group name (e.g. O2, H2O); '#' comments. With "fit per spectrum" every group gets its own strength per spectrum.</string>
                   </property>
                  </widget>
                 </item>
                 <item row="6" column="2" colspan="2">
                  <widget class="QWidget" name="row_telldetect">
                   <layout class="QHBoxLayout" name="row_telldetect_l">
                    <property name="leftMargin"><number>0</number></property>
                    <property name="topMargin"><number>0</number></property>
                    <property name="rightMargin"><number>0</number></property>
                    <property name="bottomMargin"><number>0</number></property>
                    <item>
                     <widget class="QPushButton" name="pushButton_telldetect">
                      <property name="toolTip">
                       <string>Ranges from the static spectrum of the last Solve (with static lines; best over the whole range, option above off): pixels deviating by more than the given number of sigma from a running median (5 A), widened by 0.5 A, gaps below 1 A closed; absorption and emission (sky lines). Written to &lt;file&gt;_detected.&lt;ext&gt; and set above.</string>
                      </property>
                      <property name="text">
                       <string>Detect</string>
                      </property>
                     </widget>
                    </item>
                    <item>
                     <widget class="QDoubleSpinBox" name="doubleSpinBox_telldet">
                      <property name="toolTip">
                       <string>Threshold of "Detect" in units of the noise of the static spectrum (robust, from the median absolute deviation).</string>
                      </property>
                      <property name="suffix">
                       <string> σ</string>
                      </property>
                      <property name="decimals"><number>1</number></property>
                      <property name="minimum"><double>1.0</double></property>
                      <property name="maximum"><double>50.0</double></property>
                      <property name="value"><double>5.0</double></property>
                     </widget>
                    </item>
                   </layout>
                  </widget>
                 </item>
                </layout>
               </widget>
              </item>
              <item>
               <widget class="QGroupBox" name="grpNoise">
                <property name="title">
                 <string>Noise</string>
                </property>
                <layout class="QGridLayout" name="grdNoise">
                 <item row="0" column="0">
                  <widget class="QLabel" name="lbl_15">
                   <property name="text">
                    <string>S/N of the spectra</string>
                   </property>
                  </widget>
                 </item>
                 <item row="0" column="1">
                  <widget class="QDoubleSpinBox" name="doubleSpinBox_16">
                   <property name="toolTip">
                    <string>Signal-to-noise ratio of the (continuum-normalised) spectra; noise sigma = 1/(S/N). auto: estimated from the residuum (residuum^2 / degrees of freedom).</string>
                   </property>
                   <property name="specialValueText">
                    <string>auto</string>
                   </property>
                   <property name="decimals">
                    <number>1</number>
                   </property>
                   <property name="minimum">
                    <double>0</double>
                   </property>
                   <property name="maximum">
                    <double>100000</double>
                   </property>
                   <property name="singleStep">
                    <double>10</double>
                   </property>
                   <property name="value">
                    <double>0</double>
                   </property>
                   <property name="minimumSize">
                    <size>
                     <width>90</width>
                     <height>0</height>
                    </size>
                   </property>
                   <property name="maximumSize">
                    <size>
                     <width>90</width>
                     <height>16777215</height>
                    </size>
                   </property>
                  </widget>
                 </item>
                 <item row="0" column="2" rowspan="1" colspan="2">
                  <widget class="QLabel" name="lbl_16">
                   <property name="text">
                    <string>auto: from the residuum</string>
                   </property>
                  </widget>
                 </item>
                 <item row="1" column="0" rowspan="1" colspan="2">
                  <widget class="QCheckBox" name="checkBox_41">
                   <property name="text">
                    <string>Weight per spectrum by S/N from</string>
                   </property>
                   <property name="toolTip">
                    <string>Weighted least squares: each spectrum is weighted with 1/sigma^2, sigma = 1/(S/N), S/N per spectrum from the file (one value per line, same order as the spectra). Solve writes an estimate from the residuals to snr_estimated.dat.</string>
                   </property>
                  </widget>
                 </item>
                 <item row="1" column="2" rowspan="1" colspan="2">
                  <widget class="QLineEdit" name="lineEdit_29">
                   <property name="toolTip">
                    <string>File with one S/N value per spectrum, or "auto": estimate the S/N per spectrum from the residuals (3 iterations at the first solve, written to snr_estimated.dat).</string>
                   </property>
                   <property name="text">
                    <string>snr.dat</string>
                   </property>
                  </widget>
                 </item>
                 <item row="2" column="0" colspan="2">
                  <widget class="QCheckBox" name="checkBox_align">
                   <property name="text">
                    <string>Align continua to the mean, smoothing</string>
                   </property>
                   <property name="toolTip">
                    <string>Before disentangling, each spectrum is divided by its smoothed ratio to the mean of all spectra (boxcar of the given width, applied twice; excluded ranges left out). This removes differences of the normalisation between the spectra, which the disentangling turns into broad anti-correlated wiggles of A and B. Also removes real broad differences, e.g. from shifted Balmer wings, on scales of the width and above.</string>
                   </property>
                  </widget>
                 </item>
                 <item row="2" column="2" colspan="2">
                  <widget class="QDoubleSpinBox" name="doubleSpinBox_alignWidth">
                   <property name="suffix">
                    <string> Å</string>
                   </property>
                   <property name="decimals">
                    <number>0</number>
                   </property>
                   <property name="minimum">
                    <double>5.0</double>
                   </property>
                   <property name="maximum">
                    <double>2000.0</double>
                   </property>
                   <property name="singleStep">
                    <double>5.0</double>
                   </property>
                   <property name="value">
                    <double>30.0</double>
                   </property>
                   <property name="toolTip">
                    <string>Width of the boxcar (applied twice) for the ratio of each spectrum to the mean spectrum. Must be much larger than the RV shifts of the lines (a few Å).</string>
                   </property>
                  </widget>
                 </item>
                </layout>
               </widget>
              </item>
